    "background_story": "In the 12th century, Marshall, a cunning and ambitious nobleman, carved out a vast fiefdom in the rolling hills of medieval England. Through strategic alliances and military conquests, he expanded his dominion, securing the loyalty of his vassals and the fear of his enemies. His castle, perched atop a craggy outcropping, became the seat of his power, where he dispensed justice and collected taxes from his subjects. Marshall's fiefdom flourished under his rule, with trade and agriculture thriving. He was a just and fair lord, beloved by his people, who saw him as a protector and a provider. As his reputation grew, so did his influence, earning him a place among the most powerful nobles of the realm. Marshall's fiefdom became a beacon of stability in a turbulent era, a testament to his strength and wisdom.",
